  "scientific_conclusion": "Prospective ECELLE_V3_1 optical SETI survey across 130 exposures of 26 fresh nearby FGKM stars (70 HARPS + 60 VLT ESPRESSO; 20 control exposures on 4 non-planet stars + 110 science exposures across 22 confirmed exoplanet hosts with 44 planets at 3.64-44.86 pc) completed: Legacy V2 generated 422 false alarms (346 science), D079-equivalent V3.0 pre-F1 G1 generated 153 persistent photospheric bumps + 65 Channel T V3.0 passers, while prospective V3.1 Gates G1_F1-G5_F2 yielded 10 control (0.50/exp) and 24 science (0.22/exp) survivors (no ETI laser excess), setting 8-sigma beamed 10 m transmitter upper limits of median 10.28 kW (down to 0.91 kW on HIP70849)."
